GC_LobbyGameMode : "{A79C4E0A43DEB821}Prefabs/MP/Modes/GC_LobbyGameMode.et" {
 ID "12E1DBDDC6F83EF2"
 components {
  GC_LobbyManager "{6A137A39106A4973}" {
   m_aBriefings {
    GC_Briefing "{2C66AEB4E3C99C37}" {
     m_iOrder 0
     m_sTitle "Summary"
     m_sContent "A retreating train carrying Russian troops and equipment has been ambushed by partisan forces. The tracks have been sabotaged, causing the train to derail and leaving its occupants stranded."\
     "With resistance fighters in the area and US forces in pursuit, the remaining Russian troops must organize a hasty defense and hold their position until reinforcements can arrive."\
     ""\
     "<h2>SUMMARY NOTES</h2>"\
     "• Setup timer: Blufor = 6mins. "
     m_eAudience 1
    }
    GC_Briefing "{D63EDC23E3DC7763}" {
     m_iOrder 1
     m_sTitle "Situation"
     m_sContent "<h2>PRELIMS</h2>"\
     "DTL: 27/07/2001, 0745hr, Ruha."\
     "Weather: Cloudy but dry, forcast of change, sightlines 1km +"\
     ""\
     "<h2>LORE</h2>"\
     "A Russian train with troops and equipment has been forced into retreat following the loss of control in the surrounding region. During its withdrawal, the train was ambushed by partisan resistance forces, who sabotaged the rail line and caused a derailment."\
     ""\
     "The ambush was not intended to destroy the force outright, but to delay and fix it in place. Resistance elements remain active in the area conducting harassment attacks and observing the stranded troops. The derailment has also drawn the attention of US forces, which are now advancing toward the site to exploit the situation and prevent an organized withdrawal."\
     ""\
     "Russian troops on the ground are isolated and operating with limited mobility. Reinforcements have been requested, but their arrival is uncertain. Until relief arrives, the derailed train and surrounding terrain must be held under increasing pressure."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "US"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{335245EA27DDA089}" {
     m_iOrder 2
     m_sTitle "Situation"
     m_sContent "<h2>PRELIMS</h2>"\
     "DTL: 27/07/2001, 0745hr, Ruha."\
     "Weather: Cloudy but dry, forcast of change, sightlines 1km +"\
     ""\
     "<h2>LORE</h2>"\
     "A Russian train with troops and equipment has been forced into retreat following the loss of control in the surrounding region. During its withdrawal, the train was ambushed by partisan resistance forces, who sabotaged the rail line and caused a derailment."\
     ""\
     "The ambush was not intended to destroy the force outright, but to delay and fix it in place. Resistance elements remain active in the area conducting harassment attacks and observing the stranded troops. The derailment has also drawn the attention of US forces, which are now advancing toward the site to exploit the situation and prevent an organized withdrawal."\
     ""\
     "Russian troops on the ground are isolated and operating with limited mobility. Reinforcements have been requested, but their arrival is uncertain. Until relief arrives, the derailed train and surrounding terrain must be held under increasing pressure."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "RHS_AFRF"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{F705AD9FE1667A09}" {
     m_iOrder 3
     m_sTitle "Enemy forces"
     m_sContent "<h2>COMPOSITION & DISPOSITION</h2> "\
     "Enemy forces consist of approximately 20 Russian troops from the 275th Motor Rifle Regiment. Their train was derailed at GRID: 064059 with assistance from friendly INDFOR partisan forces."\
     "Partisan reporting indicates the locomotive has been destroyed. The enemy has sustained casualties in the crash and appears to be establishing a hasty defensive position while awaiting relief."\
     "The nearest known enemy unit is the 278th Guards Motor Rifle Regiment, located approximately 5 km to our south. They are assessed as the most likely force to respond and attempt extraction of the surviving troops."\
     "<h2>STRENGTHS, CAPABILITIES & LIMITATIONS</h2> "\
     "• The train is armed. Partisan forces report a ZU-23 positioned at both the front and rear of the train. Several carriages contain fortified fighting positions, including static machine gun emplacements."\
     "• Although time is limited, the Russians will use every available moment to establish defensive positions, set kill zones, clear fields of fire, and prepare delay and fallback positions."\
     "• Enemy forces are currently dismounted. One flank of their position is fully exposed due to the adjacent lake, limiting concealed maneuver options on that side. "\
     ""\
     "<h2>SERVICE & SUPPORT</h2> "\
     "• The train was transporting heavy and light weapons, equipment, and supplies. With withdrawal no longer possible, these resources are expected to be used to reinforce their defensive posture and delay our assault."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "US"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{A011EFB604A02019}" {
     m_iOrder 4
     m_sTitle "Enemy forces"
     m_sContent "<h2>COMPOSITION & DISPOSITION</h2> "\
     "Enemy forces are assessed to be elements of the U.S. Army."\
     "Local partisan forces sabotaged the railway, causing our derailment. A brief engagement occurred immediately after the crash, after which the partisans withdrew. Their actions appear intended to delay and fix us in position until pursuing U.S. forces can close in."\
     "We should expect enemy contact from the north."\
     ""\
     "<h2>STRENGTHS, CAPABILITIES & LIMITATIONS</h2> "\
     "• Detailed information regarding the enemy’s strength, composition, and logistics (SCL) is currently unknown."\
     "• We should anticipate a numerically superior force, likely equipped with light-skinned vehicles to enable rapid maneuver and mobility."\
     "• A key enemy limitation will be their ability to approach undetected or under cover on one flank of our position due to the large, open swamp bordering the train."\
     ""\
     "<h2>SERVICE & SUPPORT</h2>"\
     "• Unknown at this time."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "RHS_AFRF"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{754CC712E21A5C81}" {
     m_iOrder 5
     m_sTitle "Friendly forces"
     m_sContent "<h2>COMPOSITION & DISPOSITION</h2> "\
     "We are Delta Company, 1st Platoon, 20th Infantry Regiment, U.S. Army."\
     "A motorized Humvee platoon consisting of 38 personnel, currently located at the staging area (GRID: 070081), preparing to step off in 5 minutes."\
     ""\
     "<h2>STRENGTHS, CAPABILITIES & LIMITATIONS</h2> "\
     "• We do <b>not</b> possess the capability to defeat a reinforcing enemy relief force. Speed and decisive action are critical."\
     "• We have freedom of movement within the AO aside from the known enemy presence. The area is otherwise uncontested, and the target unit is assessed to be isolated, allowing easier positioning with minimal resistance."\
     "• The platoon is fully mobile, with sufficient vehicles to allow each callsign to operate either mounted or dismounted as required."\
     "• The east side of the train is dominated by a large open swamp with minimal cover or concealment. The terrain is shallow and trafficable by both foot and vehicle, with multiple small low-lying islands throughout."\
     ""\
     "<h2>SERVICE & SUPPORT</h2> "\
     "• HQ Squad: 1x M2 (.50 cal) armed Humvee and 2x unarmed Humvees."\
     "• Weapons Squad: 2x unarmed Humvees."\
     "• Each Rifle Squad: 2x M2 (.50 cal) armed Humvees."\
     "• Each vehicle carries a light squad rearm, including 2x demolition charges and 1x clacker."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "US"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{D5044CB661B1754D}" {
     m_iOrder 6
     m_sTitle "Friendly forces"
     m_sContent "<h2>COMPOSITION & DISPOSITION</h2> "\
     "We are the remaining 24 Russian troops from the derailed train, elements of the 275th Motor Rifle Regiment. We were retreating by rail when partisan sabotage caused the derailment."\
     "Current location: GRID 064059."\
     "Our nearest friendly unit is the 278th Guards Motor Rifle Regiment, positioned approximately 5 km to our south. A company-sized element has been dispatched to extract us, with an estimated time of arrival of 30–40 minutes. "\
     "<h2>STRENGTHS, CAPABILITIES & LIMITATIONS</h2> "\
     "• The train is armed and up-armoured. A ZU-23 is mounted at both the front and rear. Multiple carriages and rooftop positions contain prepared fighting positions equipped with mounted machine guns."\
     "• While the immediate area is currently uncontested, we must remain aware that we are on foot with no vehicle mobility. Our ability to maneuver is limited, and any overextension without rapid withdrawal capability could prove costly."\
     "• The derailment site provides defensible terrain. One entire flank of the train is bordered by a large open swamp, offering excellent fields of fire and denying the enemy effective concealment or cover during approach. Bridges at either end of the train create natural choke points. Nearby wooded areas and buildings provide strong options for establishing delay positions or fallback defenses."\
     ""\
     "<h2>SERVICE & SUPPORT</h2> "\
     "• The train was transporting significant supplies, now scattered due to the crash. Recover and redistribute usable equipment from nearby cargo crates."\
     "• Available equipment includes a tripod-mounted NSV 12.7mm heavy machine gun, tripod-mounted AGS-17 automatic grenade launcher, launchers with ammunition, anti-tank and anti-personnel mines (including demolition charges), small arms ammunition, grenades, and fortification materials such as deployable barbed wire, sandbags, and camouflage foliage."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "RHS_AFRF"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{A0EAA0B79E8AA7AC}" {
     m_iOrder 7
     m_sTitle "Mission"
     m_sContent "<h2>MISSION STATEMENT</h2>"\
     "We are to conduct a HASTY RAID on the derailed train in order to destroy equipment caches and deny their future use by relief forces, before withdrawing from the AO."\
     ""\
     "<h2>MISSION DESCRIPTION</h2> "\
     "Friendly INDFOR partisan forces have successfully ambushed a retreating Russian train within the AO, causing it to derail."\
     "We have been rapidly deployed in pursuit to strike the crash site before a Russian quick reaction force (QRF) can arrive and extract surviving personnel or recover equipment."\
     "Once the objective is complete, we will WITHDRAW north-bound from the AO <b>beyond</b> the railway bridge."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "US"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{14FF2B910B7B420A}" {
     m_iOrder 8
     m_sTitle "Mission"
     m_sContent "<h2>MISSION STATEMENT</h2> "\
     "We are to conduct a hasty defense of the train derailment site and hold in place pending extraction by friendly forces."\
     "Estimated time of arrival: 30–40 minutes. "\
     ""\
     "<h2>EXECUTION</h2> "\
     "<b>1.</b> Recover weapons, ammunition, and equipment from the scattered supply crates."\
     "<b>2.</b> Occupy designated fighting positions and man assigned weapon systems in accordance with the Commanding Officer’s orders."\
     "<b>3.</b> Establish defensive works: dig in, emplace obstacles and fortifications, clear fields of fire, and create kill zones and engagement funnels."\
     "<b>4.</b> Maintain defensive posture and hold position until friendly forces arrive for extraction. "
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "RHS_AFRF"
     }
    }
